<title>DENMARK: Denmark's Neurosearch soars on drug test.</title>
<headline>Denmark's Neurosearch soars on drug test.</headline>
<dateline>COPENHAGEN 1997-05-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Danish biotech company Neurosearch rose by 4.83 percent on Wednesday after the company announced first clinical trials, to be held in Britain, of a new anti-anxiety medication, NS 2710.</p>
<p>At 1125 GMT the share was up 16 crowns from Tuesday's close, to 347 crowns.</p>
<p>&quot;In comparison with existing anxiety compounds NS 2710 has shown a significant anti-anxiety effect and no, or very minor, side effects in preclinical trials,&quot; a Neurosearch statement said.</p>
<p>--Steve Weizman, Copenhagen newsroom +45 33969650</p>
</text>
